 "drivingQuestion": "Why is the reading advanced and not postponed?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Answered from the verse",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "megillah.5a.9",
   "daf": "5a",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "בְּאֵלּוּ, אָמְרוּ מַקְדִּימִין וְלֹא מְאַחֲרִין. מַאי טַעְמָא? אָמַר רַבִּי אַבָּא אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: אָמַר קְרָא ״וְלֹא יַעֲבוֹר״.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «It was with regard to these» times for reading the Megilla that the Sages «said» that «one advances» the reading of the Megilla «and one does not postpone» it. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? «Rabbi Abba said» that «Shmuel said:» The «verse states:» “The Jews ordained, and took upon them, and upon their seed, and upon all who joined themselves to them, «and it shall not pass,» that they should keep these two days” (Esther 9:27), which indicates that the designated time must not pass without the reading of the Megilla."
  }
 ],
